Rating guidelines: A company that is certified 100% cruelty-free (e.g., Leaping Bunny), sources exclusively from verified humane or plant-based supply chains with zero factory farming, prohibits painful animal testing, and actively promotes biodiversity conservation gets a 100. A company that meets baseline legal animal welfare requirements and standard industry practices without third-party humane certifications gets a 50. A company that finances painful animal testing despite viable alternatives, relies heavily on extreme confinement factory farming, sources from fur or live-plucking operations, or suppresses animal cruelty exposés gets a 1.
